@@ -528,3 +528,33 @@ Project cost projection uses the existing registered local project list. Convers
 unregistered paths and null history group under Other without rewriting immutable usage facts or
 removing them from account-period allocation. Agent-editable statistics must reuse the existing
 Session/permission and Settings owners; that contextual bridge is not implemented by this change.
+
+### Activity evidence and source-backed charts
+
+Reuse the existing model_usage, turn_usage and tool_usage records and the same usage/stats query.
+The original tool_usage table already owns identity, scope, outcomes, latency, output size, retries
+and permissions. Expose its existing tool aggregate before adding counters. Skill result/error events
+already carry qualified name, plugin ID and source, but those fields are not retained in tool_usage;
+extend that row with nullable metadata, not another event stream or telemetry service. Repeated
+events upsert the same session/tool-call identity. Never infer historical skills from installed lists.
+
+The initial activity view reports tool calls and explicit Skill invocations with outcome/latency.
+Installed/enabled/loaded/executed are distinct; a loaded skill does not prove task success. Actual
+API billing remains per request. Session/turn links permit later associated-cost analysis but do not
+justify billing every tool or skill for a whole model request. Version provenance, accepted outcome,
+before/after configuration cohorts and an Agent read/write bridge still need their own real facts.
+Keep structured facts, not additional copies of prompts, credentials or complete tool output.
+
+Cost presentation follows EvilCharts' grouped horizontal bar pattern over the existing ZCode
+Recharts/ChartContainer. Model/project grouping is separate from total/per-million units. API
+estimates and allocated payments are alternative valuations, not stackable components. Unknowns
+remain gaps; different currencies use separate charts. Reuse original page order, tokens and controls.
+
+
+ReadUsageStats is a read-only tool over the same injected SessionStore usage query, bounded to 7/30
+days. It returns aggregate models/tools/identified skills and price coverage with local-host scope,
+never raw messages, credentials or configuration commands. It remains available independently of
+dynamic workflow gating. Normal tool deny/permission rules apply. It does not claim Agent settings
+editing, automatically disable plugins, change models or allocate per-tool bills. Missing port/data
+returns explicit unavailable/null instead of a fabricated empty account. Human and Agent statistics
+share the same query owner and scope semantics.
